Think: Good, the timestamps have been extracted. Now let me process each timestamp to normalize and validate them. I'll use a simple approach with awk to handle the normalization and validation.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F: '{
  hour = $1
  minute = $2

  # Normalize to HH:MM format
  normalized_hour = sprintf("%02d", hour)
  normalized_minute = sprintf("%02d", minute)
  normalized_timestamp = normalized_hour ":" normalized_minute

  # Validate 24-hour format (hour 00-23, minute 00-59)
  if (hour >= 0 && hour <= 23 && minute >= 0 && minute <= 59) {
    print normalized_timestamp >> "timestamps.txt"
  } else {
    print $0 >> "timestamps_errors.log"
  }
}' temp_timestamps.txt
```

Think: Good, that worked. Now let me process all timestamps at once using awk to normalize them and validate the 24-hour format.

Act: bash

```bash
awk -F: '{
  hour = $1; minute = $2;
  if (hour >= 0 && hour <= 23 && minute >= 0 && minute <= 59) {
    printf "%02d:%02d\n", hour, minute
  }
}' temp_timestamps.txt > timestamps.txt
```

